# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FayaNMS production environment — Docker Compose deployment (T6 of
# docs/deploy/WINDOWS-SERVER-DOCKER-DESKTOP.md).
#
# Usage:
#   cp docs/deploy/env.production.example .env.production   # then fill EVERY value
#   docker compose --env-file .env.production build
#
# This file does double duty:
#   1. compose interpolation (build args, host port) via --env-file
#   2. container runtime env via env_file (app + worker + provision services)
#
# NO usable secret ships in this repository. Generate every value per
# environment; the startup security policy FAILS production otherwise
# (src/lib/startup/security-policy.ts):
#   * NEXTAUTH_SECRET        — required, >= 32 chars, never a known/demo value
#   * FAYANMS_SERVICE_SECRET — required, 64 hex chars (internal service JWTs)
#   * FAYANMS_CONFIG_ENC_KEY — required, 64 hex chars (config-encryption KEK —
#     losing it = losing every config-snapshot backup; back it up OFF-BOX,
#     separately from the database backups)
#   * POSTGRES_PASSWORD      — required, 64 hex chars (PostgreSQL superuser of
#     the compose `postgres` service; the app DATABASE_URL is composed from it)
#   * FAYANMS_DEMO_MODE      — must NOT be "true" in production
#
# Never commit the real file (.env* is gitignored; gitleaks runs on every push).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Canonical public origin (DNS name preferred; a raw LAN IP also passes the
# siteUrl() guard — NEVER localhost / *.local). Baked into the client bundle at
# BUILD time — changing it later requires an image REBUILD, not just a restart.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://fayanms.example.corp

# NextAuth base URL — same origin as above (runtime value).
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://fayanms.example.corp

# ── Secrets (openssl rand -hex 32, FOUR times — inside WSL2) ─────────────
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=
FAYANMS_SERVICE_SECRET=
# Optional: previous service secrets accepted during rotation windows.
FAYANMS_SERVICE_SECRETS=
FAYANMS_CONFIG_ENC_KEY=
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
FAYANMS_CONFIG_ENC_KEY_ID=k1

# MUST stay empty in production. Demo seeding runs in the one-off provision
# container with an explicit -e override instead (runbook T7).
FAYANMS_DEMO_MODE=

# ── Optional compose knobs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Host port published for the app (defaults to 80). Change only if the host
# port is taken; the INTERNAL port 3000 is a hardcoded contract — never change it.
# FAYANMS_HTTP_PORT=80

# ── Internal service URLs (runbook T5) ───────────────────────────────────────
# compose.yml already wires both hops to the bridge-network DNS names below —
# uncomment ONLY for a custom topology. Defaults for bare-metal (non-compose)
# runs are the loopback contracts: WORKER_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3030 and
# NEXT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000.
# WORKER_BASE_URL=http://worker:3030   # app → worker (/health, /simulate/*)
# NEXT_BASE_URL=http://app:3000        # worker → app (persistence API)

# ── PostgreSQL (Phase 21 slice 1) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL is intentionally NOT set here by default: compose composes it
# from POSTGRES_PASSWORD as postgresql://fayanms:<pw>@postgres:5432/fayanms
# and points the app + provision services at the `postgres` service. Only set
# DATABASE_URL explicitly if you point the stack at an EXTERNAL PostgreSQL
# (e.g. a managed instance) — it must start with postgresql:// (the startup
# security policy enforces this), and the compose `postgres` service can be
# removed in that case.

# ── LIVE_SSH device vault (Phase 22 slice 1) ────────────────────────────────
# Devices with dataSource=LIVE_SSH are reached by the WORKER over real SSH
# (read-only). The app stores only the vault REFERENCE (CredentialProfile
# .secretRef, "vault://…"); the WORKER resolves it worker-side from entries
# in THIS file (its env_file) using the naming rule:
#   vault://ssh/network-admin  →  FAYANMS_VAULT_SSH_NETWORK_ADMIN
# Add one entry per vault reference you intend to use on live devices.
# NEVER commit this file; rotate with the credential (CredentialProfile
# .lastRotatedAt is the rotation ledger).
# FAYANMS_VAULT_SSH_NETWORK_ADMIN=
